# Browser
# A text-changing spell asks two words as it resolves (CR 612.1, 608.2d): the one to replace, then the one replacing it, and
# Bot1's page says which it is asking. Sleight of Mind on Bot2's White Knight asks "choose the color word to replace" and
# then "choose the color word that replaces it" (black, then red: the Knight has protection from red, CR 612.2); Magical
# Hack on Bot2's Plains asks "choose the basic land type to replace" and "choose the basic land type that replaces it"
# (Plains, then Island: the Plains is an Island, CR 305.6).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Island
Sleight of Mind
Magical Hack
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
White Knight
Plains x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.White Knight.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sleight of Mind.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.White Knight)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Sleight of Mind: choose the color word to replace
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = Every instance of it in the target's text is replaced
Bot1.Colors(Black)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Sleight of Mind: choose the color word that replaces it
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Magical Hack.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Plains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Magical Hack: choose the basic land type to replace
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = Every instance of it in the target's text is replaced
Bot1.Modes(Plains)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Magical Hack: choose the basic land type that replaces it
Bot1.Modes(Island)

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.White Knight.ProtectionFrom = Red
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Subtypes = Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Magical Hack; Sleight of Mind
